# probe-10 minus_unexercised
# GAP: SPARQL MINUS has ZERO corpus members (the two "negation" members q017/q053 are both
#   FILTER NOT EXISTS, which has different variable-scoping semantics). MINUS recurses in the
#   rewrite (rewrite.rs:175-196 lowers the inner triples) but the anti-join itself is generic
#   and MinusOperator has no set_row_budget (swallows the LIMIT). This probe establishes
#   whether MINUS on virtual (a) returns correct rows and (b) how the negated fact side is
#   executed (single materialize vs per-row correlate).
# MECHANISM that SHOULD fire: batched anti-join (cf. correlated-OPTIONAL PR-4b/4c/4d); MINUS
#   is NOT known to share that batching.
# PREDICTED: correct rows; DIM_CUSTOMER driver is small so wall is modest, but the negated
#   side's execution (scan_table count) reveals whether MINUS reuses the OPTIONAL batching.
PREFIX edw: <http://ns.fluree.dev/edw#>
SELECT ?cid
FROM <enterprise-sf01-v:main>
WHERE { ?c a edw:Customer ; edw:customerId ?cid ; edw:isCurrent true .
        MINUS { ?c edw:isCurrent false . } }
LIMIT 5000
